  "script": "The Mercedes Maybach S680 4MATIC flaunts an elongated chrome grille with vertical slats, a hallmark of elite luxury. A stunning two-tone paint scheme of deep blue and silver graces the Maybach, marking it as the epitome of luxury design. From the rear, a glossy black contrasts with the sleek silver roof, enhancing the Maybach\u2019s luxurious stance. Under the hood, the Maybach S680 packs a formidable 6.0-liter V12 engine, delivering 621 horsepower and 738 lb-ft of torque. The interior is adorned in two-tone blue leather, with diamond-stitching on the seats and panels, typifying Maybach's commitment to opulence. In the rear, diamond-quilted leather seats with plush headrests and embroidered Maybach logos emphasize supreme comfort. The front seats mirror this detail with exquisite diamond-stitched leather, showcasing both luxury and craftsmanship. Its 4MATIC all-wheel-drive system ensures optimal power distribution for unmatched driving stability and confidence. Originally priced around $230K, the Maybach S680 holds value well, reselling near $200K today, a modest depreciation of roughly 2.5% annually. Does the Maybach\u2019s unparalleled luxury justify its price, or does opulence have no limits? Tell us what you think.",
